WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.388
To close, the guide's checklist.

2
00:00:02.388 --> 00:00:06.216
Every account kept on Kerberos is
scored against the Identity pillar,

3
00:00:06.216 --> 00:00:07.687
with its end date and owner.

4
00:00:07.687 --> 00:00:12.829
Every Kerberos application published
through Private Access or application proxy

5
00:00:12.829 --> 00:00:14.857
names its service account and S P N,

6
00:00:14.857 --> 00:00:18.188
and the connector's delegation
entry moves with any S P N.

7
00:00:18.188 --> 00:00:21.505
S P N exclusions for
service-to-service Kerberos are in the

8
00:00:21.505 --> 00:00:25.513
exception register before the domain
controller sensor is enforced.

9
00:00:25.513 --> 00:00:29.900
Every SQL Server instance that takes
Entra logins has a T L S certificate

10
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.662
from a certificate authority,
which the service account can read.

11
00:00:33.662 --> 00:00:38.775
No service account uses N T
L M after April first, 2027.

12
00:00:38.775 --> 00:00:43.606
And the program's people sign in to AWS,
O C I and Linux hosts with Entra I D,

13
00:00:43.606 --> 00:00:48.437
while workloads use their platform's
identity, each joined to a record.

14
00:00:48.437 --> 00:00:51.109
For the moves themselves,
go back to the track:

15
00:00:51.109 --> 00:00:55.800
the Non-Person Identity implementation
guide, and the service accounts guide.

16
00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:56.690
Thank you.
